"S´eminaire Lotharingien de Combinatoire 91 (2025), Article B91b (https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~slc/wpapers/s91alia.pdf)\nciteturn6search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; Following [2], we deﬁne an abelian group G to possess the weak acyclic matching ... Theorem 2.3 classiﬁes all abelian groups with respect to their adherence to the weak\nTHE WEAK ACYCLIC MATCHING PROPERTY IN ABELIAN GROUPS\n3\nFollowing [2], we deﬁne an abelian group G to possess the weak acyclic matching\nproperty if, for every ﬁnite nonempty subsets A and B of G with |A| = |B| and\nA ∩(A + B) = ∅, A is acyclically matched to B. In [2], the following conjecture\nconcerning the weak acyclic matching property was proposed.\nConjecture 1.5. There are inﬁnitely many n for which Z/nZ has the weak acyclic\nmatching property.\nThe following question was also raised in [1].\nQuestion 1.6. Does Z/pZ possess the weak acyclic matching property for every\nprime p?\nIn this note, our main result, stated as Theorem 2.3, provides an aﬃrmative\nanswer to Conjecture 1.5 and thoroughly addresses Question 1.6.\nFurthermore,\nTheorem 2.3 classiﬁes all abelian groups with respect to their adherence to the weak\nacyclic matching property.\nRemark 1.7. It is worth noting that while the matching theory developed in this\npaper is related to the classical theory introduced by Philip Hall in 1935, the two\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAbdus Salam, GC University Report 2018.cdr (https://www.sms.edu.pk/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/Abdus-Salam-GC-University-Report-2018.pdf)\nciteturn6search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7.4 years ago; Crawled: 7.2 years ago; Finally, we introduce the notion of decomposable clutter and we show that chordality of these clutters is indeed a generalization of Simon’s conjecture on extendable shellability of d-skeletons of an n-simplex, for all d.\nShort Seminar Series\n\nALGEBRAIC APPROACH TO THE CHORDALITY OF HYPERGRAPHS\n\nAli Akbar YAZDAN POUR  \nInstitute for Advanced Studies in Basic Sciences (IASBS), IRAN\n\nTalk-I  \nFriday at 14:30 (21 December, 2018)\n\nTalk-II  \nWednesday at 14:00 (26 December, 2018)\n\nTalk-III  \nThursday at 14:00 (27 December, 2018)\n\nIn the series of three lectures, first, we review the current results on the subject of chordality. Then, we introduce some operations (called reductions) on a given (hyper)graph G to obtain a smaller (hyper)graph such that the non-linear strand Betti numbers do not change under these operations. Using these operations, we introduce a new class of d-uniform clutters (called chordal clutter) which coincides with the definition of chordal graphs in the case d = 2, and the corresponding circuit ideal has a linear resolution over any field K. Then, the graded minimal free resolution of such hypergraphs will be investigated. It is shown that these numbers are completely characterized in terms of the combinatorics of the given clutter. Finally, we introduce the notion of decomposable clutter and we show that chordality of these clutters is indeed a generalization of Simon’s conjecture on extendable shellability of d-skeletons of an n-simplex, for all d. We then prove this conjecture for d ≥ n − 3.\n\nNATIONAL CENTER FOR MATHEMATICS,  \nABDUS SALAM SCHOOL OF MATHEMATICAL  \nSCIENCES, GC UNIVERSITY, LAHORE--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBoardman–Vogt resolutions and bar/cobar constructions of (co)operadic (co)bimodules 317 (https://pure.mpg.de/rest/items/item_3366505/component/file_3366506/content)\nciteturn6search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.8 years ago; Crawled: 4.7 years ago; **Theorem 2.3** ([19, Section 8.4]). ... - *the weak equivalences are morphisms that form a weak equivalence in each arity,* ... Here, \\(\\mathcal M(\\mathcal O)(n)\\) is the matching object* ... - *cofibrations are characterized by the left lifting property with respect to the class of acyclic fibrations.\nBoardman–Vogt resolutions and bar/cobar constructions of (co)operadic (co)bimodules 317\n\nA 1-reduced Λ-operad \\(\\mathcal O\\) is the data of a 1-reduced Λ-sequence together with operadic operations (1) compatible with the Λ-structure (see [19]). The category of 1-reduced Λ-operads, denoted by ΛOperad, is endowed with an adjunction:\n\\[\n\\mathcal F:\\Lambda\\mathrm{Seq}_{>1}\\rightleftarrows\\Lambda\\mathrm{Operad}:\\mathcal U,\n\\tag{3}\n\\]\nwhere \\(\\mathcal F\\) is the left adjoint of the forgetful functor \\(\\mathcal U\\).\n\nLet us remark that, by restricting to bijections, any Λ-sequence is also a symmetric sequence. In particular, any Λ-operad has an underlying Σ-operad by restricting the action to bijections.\n\n**Theorem 2.3** ([19, Section 8.4]). *The category of 1-reduced Λ-operads ΛOperad is equipped with a model category structure such that:*\n\n- *the weak equivalences are morphisms that form a weak equivalence in each arity,*\n- *the fibrations are morphisms \\(\\phi:\\mathcal O_1\\to\\mathcal O_2\\) whose induced maps \\(\\mathcal O_1(n)\\to\\mathcal M(\\mathcal O_1)(n)\\wedge_{\\mathcal M(\\mathcal O_2)(n)}\\mathcal O_2(n)\\) are fibration maps. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEuroCG 2017, Malmö, Sweden, April 5–7, 2017 (https://computational-geometry.org/abstracts/eurocg/2017.pdf)\nciteturn6search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9.6 years ago; **Remark 6** The previous proposition shows that a TD-Delaunay complex of H_d has Dushnik-Miller dimension d.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGraph Theory · Prove2Me (https://prove2.me/f/graph-theory?page=2&status=completed)\nciteturn6search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; ### Goal: Theorem 2.3 (p. ... Part (1) of the proof of Theorem 2.3 (p. 178): for an odd hole $C$C and $i \\in C$i∈C, the deletion and contraction of $i$i in the odd hole constraint are valid for $\\mathrm{FRAC}(G)$FRAC(G).\n----------